A3. Claim 3 (g-operator)
==============================================================================
  CONFIRMED: A!B! is the unique SYMMETRIC solution; without symmetry f(A,B)=A!B!*5^(A-B-1) (A>B) also
             satisfies f=AB f(A-1,B-1) and f(1,B)=B!, so 'symmetric' in Lemma 4.1 is load-bearing.
             (AgA=(A!)^2 holds for every solution, since f(A,A)=(A!)^2 f(0,0) and f(0,0)=1 from f(1,1)=1.)

