AUDIT SUMMARY
==============================================================================
  CONFIRMED: A1 (identity/repair/flows), A2 (simplex laws), A3 (g-operator; 'symmetric' load-bearing),
    A4 (census; note 35,39 also absent at n=6), A5 (Bang/Zsigmondy/Cipolla; wild_typing lane already has it),
    A6 (3-cycle), A7 counts (248/535/287/20341/cells/null/z/shifted windows/ladder values), A8 table, A9.
  REFUTED AS STATED: section 8's 'the excess is entirely Lemma 8.2 ... explained 93, unexplained none' --
    the criterion holds for all 20341 distinct peaks (k=1 is the immediate predecessor), so it is vacuous.
  TRUE MECHANISM (FINITE-EXACT): distinct peaks below the seed box have 9 | p+1 at the null rate;
    peaks above the box are biased to 9 | p+1 (ladder ancestors are small); conditional on 9 | p+1 alone the
    -1 square window is still observed 93 vs expected 52.4 (z=5.62), because s odd forces 8 | s^2-1 and no
    peak is 6 mod 8 (peak rates 0.688 / 0.889 / 0 / 0.685 on 2 / 8 / 14 / 20 mod 24).  Stratifying by
    (dyadic range, q mod 24, v_3(q+1)) puts BOTH windows at chance: -1 window 93 vs 88.7 (z=0.46), +1 window 99 vs 100.9 (z=-0.19).
  NEW EXACT CONTENT (elementary): peaks are 2,8,20 mod 24; unique seed iff 9 !| p+1; ladder = odd-preimage chain of length v_3(p+1).
  WRONG LABEL: '37+59=96 is the classical total stopping time' -> 96 is the stopping time; 111 is total.

